// Tag vocabulary. Every tag a rule mentions must appear here, because an
// undeclared tag is the silent no-op this language exists to prevent.
//
// Bits are handed out by prefix at declaration time, so all of trained.flight.*
// lands on one contiguous run and a wildcard clause compiles to a single mask.
// A prefix group is reserved whole, which makes the group size a per-prefix
// content limit as well as the global one.

// The entry point. A brand-new player holds nothing at all, and the one rule
// that matches on nothing is what points them at their first master.
tag  quest.firstMaster

tag  training.begun

tag  trained.flight.hover
tag  trained.flight.endurance

tag  trained.aura.sustain

tag  trained.gravity.tier1

tag  trained.rhogan.greeting
tag  trained.rhogan.flight

tag  trained.oberak.greeting
tag  trained.oberak.gravity

tag  seen.firstAscension

// The Budokai. budokai.entry is the tournament's entry requirement, granted by
// the lesson that unlocks the first ascension in either half of the training
// arc, so it is earnable inside a first session. world.round.inProgress is a
// WORLD tag - the "world." prefix is what makes g_training.c set it on the
// shared set rather than on the player who tripped the rule.

tag  budokai.entry

tag  seen.budokai

tag  world.round.inProgress
